  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the steward of the capture corpus, I want the anonymizer's REST checks to accept the two valid answers they refuse today, so that the facts #830 and #285 established are published as captures instead of described in prose.\n\n### Problem\n\n`tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py check --corpus` refuses two real HFR answers with \"rest-bucket check: list not aliased\":\n1. **The empty flag bucket** answered to a request with no cookies (#830, PR #872): 223 bytes, `results_count` 0, `resources: []`. The check requires at least 2 aliased entries, so an empty bucket cannot be published. `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` §6c (LOT-057) describes it in prose only, as pending publication.\n2. **The logged-in sub-category list** (#285, PR #873): it differs from the anonymous answer by three more links, and is refused by the same bucket check.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Teach the REST checks to accept an empty bucket (no entry to alias) and the logged-in sub-category shape, with a test for each case, both accepted and still-refused (a bucket with an unaliased entry must still fail).\n- Publish both answers as captures (Mac), then turn the two \"pending publication\" notes of §6c into **verified** facts citing them.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `anonymize.py check` accepts the two shapes, and the tests show it refused them before.\n- [ ] Both captures are published; HFR-PROTOCOL §6c cites them.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
